==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|frm|conscription}}, from {{der|en|la|cōnscriptiō||levying of troops}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kənˈskɹɪpʃən/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-conscription.wav|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# [[involuntary|Involuntary]] labor, especially [[military]] service, demanded by some established authority.
#: {{syn|en|draft}}
# An enrolling or registering.
#* {{RQ:Burnet Church of England|passage='''conscription''' of men of war}}

